  "label": "Antisemitic Stereotype: Jewish people as a burden on society",
  "description": "This stereotype implies that Jewish people, particularly children, are an unnecessary or burdensome group requiring special, isolated treatment or accommodations. It is a form of antisemitism that portrays Jewish communities as a social or economic burden, often used to justify exclusion or segregation. The meme's text 'they have no where to live' and 'makes special camp spots just for them' directly invokes this harmful trope.",
